WARNING! SPOILERS (and mild flames) ahead.


Arromdee's post to correct our misconceptions had some things we missed, but
also spread several misconceptions itself, so this is a correction to his
corrections.  We appreciate being told where we messed up, but we would
also appreciate it if posters would not be so smug about things, especially
when they're wrong.  Where I have made corrections, I have tested for its
veracity.  This is edited to save space.

arromdee writes:
}Just to correct a few misconceptions....
}In article <2182@wheaton.UUCP> kroth@wheaton.UUCP (Ken Roth) writes:
>Priest:     ...    Has extra kicking abilities - useful 
>            at low levels since Priests don't use weapons well until they
>            are fifth level or so.  ...
}All characters use weapons equally well, after allowing for strength,
}weapon bonuses, etc....
Of course, stupid.  Priests just don't have these stats below level 5

>Chr (Charisma):  [deleted comments, incl. one about Elbereth]
}[no effect on Elbereth]
Probably true.  That's why it said maybe.

>   3. Sacrifice on a non-co-aligned altar.
>         success = 25%, experience level 1 and increases such that
>         success = 100% for experience level 6.
}This is wrong.  The applicable code is
}		    if (rn2(8 + (int)u.ulevel) > 5) {
}There is always a chance of it not working, though it's more likely to work
}with high experience.
huh? I don't really know.  Works well enough though.

>The minute you eat a pet, every monster on the level will head for you with 
>blood in its eye(s).  That is, you gain an intrinsic: Aggravate monster
}Not true.  Aggravate monster does not affect peaceful monsters, and peaceful
}monsters are _not_ going to suddenly attack you (as the above implies).
Get real.  The number of peaceful monsters in the game are so small that it
doesn't really matter.  For the literary impaired: Just about every monster
on the level will head for you.  And they won't actually have blood in their
eyes either, that too is just a figure of speech.  It means they want to
hurt you.

>6:  A wand of cancellation....if you zap yourself with it....will remove
>    all intrinsics.
}It won't remove intrinsics.
True.  We noticed that a short time after we posted.

>7:  Having a monster steal cursed items.  Nymphs will steal cursed armor[etc]
}Also, succubi/incubi will remove certain cursed items.
>9:  If you eat a tin of deep-fried monster meat, your rings, gloves, and 
>    weapon will fall on the floor even if these are cursed.
}Not true (fixed long ago, unless HARD isn't defined)
thanks for pointing these out.

>Note that there is approximately a 95% chance of losing a ring if you drop
>it down a sink.  However, if you kick the sink enough (ctrl-d) you have
>some chance of getting the ring back.  ...
}Not true.  You'll get _a_ ring, but it's probably not going to be the one you
}put in.
We said "some chance" of getting the ring back, and that is true.  It is
also true that you can get a new ring from the sink (that simply was not in
the spoilers)

>Cursed and blessed wands function no differently from ordinary wands.
}They have a small chance of exploding.
OK.  Neat.  But does this really mean blessed wands have a small chance of 
exploding?  Anyway, it's a very small chance.

>[list of named weapons deleted]
}A few remarks: [deleted]
It is true that this list is not entirely correct.  it is meant only as
a general guide.  That is why we included a warning that was deleted here to
the effect that it was probably wrong.

>| lump of royal jelly |   0 | 1 | 200 | Increases strength          |
}And heals and fixes bad legs.
I think this is right, but redundant

>| slice of pizza      |  75 | 1 | 250 |                             |
>| slime mold          |  75 | 1 | 250 |                             |
}Slices of pizza no longer exist after slime molds were added.
All I can say is it's a shame, a real shame, that pizza is gone.  It was one
of my favourite parts about v.2.3

>| gelatinous cube  |  10 |  100 |                                            |
>| quivering blob   |  10 |  100 |                                            |
}Many intrinsics are possible.
I had suspected this, and also for a homonculus (sp?), but I had no proof.

>| quantum mechanic |  20 |  200 | toggles speed (fast/normal), aggr monsters |
}Doesn't aggravate monsters.
You're right.  My bad.

>| zombie           |   3 |   30 |                                            |
}Depends on corpse of whatever kind of zombie it was.  (Same for mummies).
True.  (We had some problems with the food list because our latest real list
was for v.2.3

>Extra healing
>   Reg. - Heals you (or adds 4 points to max. if at max.)
}2 points.
correct, and blessed adds 5

>Object detection
>   Reg. - You are shown where objects are on level.
>          "You sense the presence of objects."
>          "You have a strange feeling." (if no objects on level)
}Cursed: any mimics disguised as objects know where you are.
Neat-o!  Kind of obscure though.

>   Note that all rings increase your food consumptions to varying degrees.
}+0 rings don't.
sorry, we didn't scrounge around in the code.

>Shock resistance 
>   No more "Died of System Shock."  Useful when polymorphing. 
}Sigh.  Will rumors never cease?  Shock resistance has absolutely nothing to do
}with system shock.  Shock resistance protects against electrical damage.
}To protect against system shock, wear a ring of polymorph control.
I don't know how this got in there, but will rumours never cease?  a ring of
polymorph control is not a safeguard against system shock.

>Remove curse
>   Reg. - Removes curses and stickeycurses on worn items.
}"Stickeycursed" is a term from an earlier spoiler list which referred to you
}being unable to remove/unwield cursed items.  This is really the _only_ type of
}curse there is, and shouldn't be given a different name.
This is probably directly from one of those earlier spoilers, but who cares
about the lack of difference?

There was some more stuff that was listed that we'll check up on and change
if we had the info wrong.  If anyone noticed wrong info, or knows additional
info that could be included, please mail, but please, we don't like smug
people.

